      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>Any biometric (e.g. fingerprint, iris, or face) on the device that meets or exceeds the requirements for Class 2 (formerly Weak), as defined by the Android CDD.</para>
          <para>Note that this is a superset of BIOMETRIC_STRONG and is defined such that BIOMETRIC_STRONG | BIOMETRIC_WEAK == BIOMETRIC_WEAK.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/hardware/biometrics/BiometricManager.Authenticators#BIOMETRIC_WEAK" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.hardware.biometrics.BiometricManager.Authenticators.BIOMETRIC_WEAK</code>.</a></format></para>
          <para>Portions of this page are modifications based on work created and shared by the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies" title="Android Open Source Project">Android Open Source Project</a></format> and used according to terms described in the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/" title="Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License">Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License.</a></format></para>
        </summary>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
