      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>Any biometric (e.g. fingerprint, iris, or face) on the device that falls short of the requirements for Class 3 (formerly Strong), as defined by the Android CDD.</para>
          <para>For example, this includes a biometric that satisfies BIOMETRIC_WEAK but does not reach BIOMETRIC_STRONG.</para>
          <para>This constant is intended to be used by public methods like BiometricManager.getBiometricSensorStrengths for obscuration.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/hardware/biometrics/BiometricManager.Authenticators#LESS_THAN_STRONG" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.hardware.biometrics.BiometricManager.Authenticators.LESS_THAN_STRONG</code>.</a></format></para>
